Option 2: Use a Service Principal Secret (Simpler)

If you want to authenticate using a client secret, use the creds input instead of client-secret.

Step 1: Create a JSON credential
#in setting we will go to security and quality ----secret and varaibles ---selection action

Run:

az ad sp create-for-rbac \
  --name github-terraform \
  --role Contributor \
  --scopes /subscriptions/<subscription-id> \
  --json-auth

Example output:

{
  "clientId": "...",
  "clientSecret": "...",
  "subscriptionId": "...",
  "tenantId": "..."
}
Step 2: Store it as one GitHub secret

Create a repository secret:

AZURE_CREDENTIALS

Paste the entire JSON into that secret.
